# Swift Chat License

Version 1.0, September 2026. Copyright © Union Street Studios, LLC.

Swift Chat is free to use and closed source, the same way Apple distributes its own binary frameworks.

## What you can do

- Use Swift Chat in any number of apps, including commercial apps, at no charge.
- Ship those apps to end users on any Apple platform Swift Chat supports.
- Use it in internal tools, prototypes, staging builds, and client work.
- Keep using any version you have already integrated, forever.

## What you cannot do

- Redistribute Swift Chat on its own, as source or binary, or bundle it in another SDK, framework, or developer tool. It may only ship embedded inside your app.
- Decompile, disassemble, reverse engineer, or otherwise attempt to derive the source code, except where applicable law expressly permits it despite this restriction.
- Remove or alter copyright notices.
- Use Swift Chat to build a general-purpose chat SDK or hosted chat service that competes with it.

## Source access

Teams that need the source, custom terms, or integration help can write to hello@unionst.com. Source provided under a separate agreement stays confidential to the receiving organization.

## No warranty

Swift Chat is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including the warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. In no event shall Union Street Studios, LLC be liable for any claim, damages, or other liability arising from the use of Swift Chat.

## Termination

This license ends automatically if you breach it. On termination, stop distributing new builds that include Swift Chat. Apps already in users' hands are unaffected.

